      "message": "This can be replaced with `MaskFormat maskFormat \u003d buffer.read32LE(MaskFormat::kLast);`, and you don\u0027t necessarily need to immediately check for validate() since `SkReadBuffer` will remember until the end, so as long as nothing in this deserialization function really would use the zero\u0027ed value returned on invalid from read32LE, we\u0027d catch it in one of the more explicit validate state checks.",
