        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-28T15:23:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have a slight preference when a magic constant is only used in one place to not actually define far from that place.\n\nIn the cases of the sub runs, we have 3 different subclasses that all define the same variable name, which could be confusing if you don\u0027t realize their scope. In the SDF case, the magic constant is just aliasing an existing constant (so using that in both the bounds and in glyphSrcPadding() seems fine); in the direct case, the constant is just 0 (in which case seeing 0 emphasizes there is no actual insetting or padding); in the transformed case, since have padding in glyphSrcPadding() but not in the bounds function, I think narrowing the scope to just the `make_vertex_filler` call with a comment saying that we don\u0027t inset these bounds but do addd padding when placed in an atlas, would be the clearest.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 752,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 752,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "974c06f41a6d4c4092c2cb1c1dec7a0114b7b263",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
